 "title": "SN55LBC176, SN65LBC176, SN65LBC176Q, SN75LBC176: 5 V half-duplex RS-485 differential bus transceivers",
 "source": {
  "document": "SLLS067I",
  "revision": "Revision I, October 2022",
  "pages": 29
 },
 "summary": "A single-supply 5 V RS-485/RS-422 transceiver with one differential driver and one differential receiver sharing the A/B bus pins. The driver enable DE is active high and the receiver enable RE active low, so the two can be tied into one direction line; with both off the part draws 200 µA at most (250 µA for SN55LBC176 and SN65LBC176Q). The receiver has ±200 mV sensitivity, 50 mV typical hysteresis and an open-input failsafe; the driver is current limited and the die has thermal shutdown. Four temperature grades come in SOIC-8, PDIP-8, CDIP-8 and a 20-pad LCCC.",
 "key_figures": [
  [
   "Supply",
   "4.75 V to 5.25 V"
  ],
  [
   "Bus common-mode range",
   "–7 V to 12 V recommended"
  ],
  [
   "Driver output |VOD2|",
   "1.1 V min into 54 Ω (1.5 V min, SN75LBC176)"
  ],
  [
   "Receiver thresholds",
   "±0.2 V, hysteresis 50 mV typ"
  ],
  [
   "Driver delay td(OD)",
   "8 ns to 25 ns (SN65/SN75), 31 ns max (SN55/SN65Q)"
  ],
  [
   "Receiver delay tPLH, tPHL",
